      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors describe a clinic case regarding a 23 year-old man affected by an osteoid osteoma of the hip's posterior edge of the cotyloid cavity. The illness had been treated for two years as a lumbar disc syndrome. As any objective clinic sign missed at the hip's level and given the rarity of the location, only surgical removal was able to cure the patient."},
